<title>JAPAN: Mitsui to supply telecom gear to Sri Lanka.</title>
<headline>Mitsui to supply telecom gear to Sri Lanka.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-05-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Japan's Mitsui &amp; Co said on Tuesday that it had won a 4.5 billion yen contract to supply switchboards, transmission equipment and cable to state-run Sri Lanka Telecom.</p>
<p>It said the project would involve adding 68,000 new lines in Colombo.</p>
<p>The Japanese trading house said it would buy the switchboards and transmission equipment from NEC Corp and the fibre optics and copper cable from South Korea's LG Cable &amp; Machinery Ltd.</p>
<p>It said the installment of the equipment was expected to be completed by early 1999.</p>
</text>
